From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:15:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 164/225] Bluetooth: add btsprdsdio HCI driver for Marlin3-Lite
 SDIO

Native hci0 for the external SC2355 WCN combo over the sprdwcn SDIO bus.
Forked from btsprdsipc: keeps the hci_dev setup, H4 RX reassembly and the
Unisoc pskey/RF/enable vendor-command init sequence; swaps the transport
from rpmsg/SIPC to the sprdwcn SDIO mchn bus (BT_TX chn 3 / BT_RX chn 17,
start_marlin(MARLIN_BLUETOOTH), push_list/mchn RX), bound to sprd,mtty.

The pskey/RF config is parsed in-kernel from the vendor text INI
(btsprd_ini.c) for parity with the Wi-Fi path. Clears the LMP Park feature
bit the SC2355 firmware advertises but rejects in a default link policy.
The BD address is derived from the SoC die UID (efuse uid-start/uid-end)
for a stable, per-unit locally-administered address, with a random fallback.

Scanning and pairing verified on device (hci0 up, classic + LE).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
